      "body": "At a glance\n\nTransport Fever 3 editions on Steam currently show a Standard tier and a Deluxe tier with a Steam key signal visible to buyers; the Collector's, Limited, and Ultimate tier names are not announced as of 2026-09-28 and should be checked on the official store page for any update. Pricing varies by regional storefront and currency, so always reconfirm the local price on Steam before purchase. Research date for this comparison is 2026-09-28.\n\nTransport Fever 3 Standard and Deluxe tier overview\n\nThe Steam store page for Transport Fever 3 lists a Standard tier that grants the launch build on September 29, 2026 and a Deluxe tier that typically bundles a Steam key with the base game plus additional launch-day content. Deluxe perks historically on similar Transport Fever releases include soundtrack, digital art book, and cosmetic vehicle skins, but the exact Deluxe contents for Transport Fever 3 should be confirmed on the live Steam store page because publishers frequently revise Deluxe offerings up to launch day.\n\nThe Deluxe edition is the closest confirmed option for buyers who want extras on launch day. If the publisher adds a Collector, Limited, or Ultimate tier later, the Steam store page will list it as a separate SKU; this page updates only after that signal appears in an authoritative source.\n\nEdition comparison table\n\n| Edition tier | Availability as of 2026-09-28 | Confirmed contents | Best for |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Standard | Available on Steam | Base game (launch build, Early Access) | Players who only want the launch build |\n| Deluxe | Available on Steam (Steam key signal) | Base game + Deluxe extras (soundtrack, art book, vehicle skins historically) | Players who want launch-day extras |\n| Collector's | Not announced as of 2026-09-28 | Not announced as of 2026-09-28; check the official Steam store page for updates | Buyers waiting on a confirmed Collector bundle |\n| Limited | Not announced as of 2026-09-28 | Not announced as of 2026-09-28; check the official Steam store page for updates | Buyers waiting on a confirmed Limited run |\n| Ultimate | Not announced as of 2026-09-28 | Not announced as of 2026-09-28; check the official Steam store page for updates | Buyers waiting on a confirmed Ultimate tier |\n\nThe table above records only what the Steam store page currently shows. Any additional tier (Collector, Limited, Ultimate, or platform-specific edition) must be added with the exact contents once the publisher confirms them on the Steam store page.\n\nRegional pricing notes and currency scope\n\nSteam regional pricing varies by storefront, currency, and tax treatment. A US-dollar price on the en-US storefront is not the same number as a euro price on a European storefront or a pound price on the UK storefront. Buyers should always check their local Steam storefront before completing a purchase, especially during the pre-order window leading up to the September 29, 2026 launch.\n\nFor players who pre-order through Steam, the regional price locks at the pre-order time and the local currency is charged at launch. Cross-region gift purchases are subject to Steam gift restrictions, so edition choice should match the recipient's regional storefront to avoid activation issues.\n\nHow Transport Fever 3 editions relate to pre-order and launch\n\nThe pre-order guide explains the Steam pre-order bonus and which edition tiers ship with pre-order incentives on day one. The release date status page tracks the September 29, 2026 launch window and the Early Access flag, both of which apply to every edition tier. The platforms page covers platform-specific edition availability, and the Steam store reference carries the AppID, supported languages, and community hub in one place.\n\nEdition contents on the Steam store page are the source of truth; this comparison page summarizes the live signal as of 2026-09-28 and flags any tier the publisher has not yet confirmed."
